//api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":13176832,"digest":"sha256:7c1f49bf9f22f15f684ce1dcc76768f04b5dc3795281aef750d1e5ad78ff1459","download_count":234,"created_at":"2026-09-09T12:25:40Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T12:25:42Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next/releases/download/v2.7.5/aria2-next-2.7.5-windows-x86_64.exe"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next/tarball/v2.7.5","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next/zipball/v2.7.5","body":"## Summary\n\nImproves parallel HTTP downloads through signed redirect links and over uneven IPv4/IPv6 paths, reduces slow completion tails, and fixes Windows event-loop crashes and CRLF input handling. No CLI, RPC, or saved-state migration is required.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Reuse validated redirect destinations for subsequent ranges instead of repeatedly requesting the original signed entry URL. Refresh rejected destinations through a single in-flight request per source route while preserving healthy transfers and retry delays.\n- Let idle workers split the largest unfinished range without waiting for a throughput sample. Small stalled tails can now be reassigned even when they have received fewer than 64 KiB.\n- Preserve the earliest requested event-loop wakeup so a later libcurl timer cannot postpone work already due.\n- Fix a Windows event-loop crash caused by inconsistent Winsock header initialization across translation units.\n- Parse CRLF input lists without retaining carriage returns that interfere with blank lines and per-download options.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Share one range queue across bounded IPv4/IPv6 workers for unrestricted parallel HTTP downloads. Workers retain their address-family choice across ranges, allowing faster workers to take more work without switching other active transfers. Existing connection limits and explicit network settings remain effective.\n- Preserve the original origin boundary for HTTP credentials and manually supplied Authorization and Cookie headers when opening ranges directly at a cached redirect destination. Cookie storage and connection reuse remain managed by libcurl.\n\n### Added\n\n- Native Windows x64 HTTP validation support, with regression scenarios for single-use redirects, expired destinations, cross-origin credentials, and changing dual-stack transfer speeds.\n\n### Downloads\n\n| Platform | Asset |\n| --- | --- |\n| Linux x86_64 | `aria2-next-2.7.5-linux-x86_64` |\n| Linux ARM64 | `aria2-next-2.7.5-linux-aarch64` |\n| macOS Apple Silicon | `aria2-next-2.7.5-macos-arm64` |\n| macOS Intel | `aria2-next-2.7.5-macos-x86_64` |\n| Windows x86_64 | `aria2-next-2.7.5-windows-x86_64.exe` |\n| Windows ARM64 | `aria2-next-2.7.5-windows-arm64.exe` |\n| Android ARM64 | `aria2-next-2.7.5-android-arm64` |\n| SHA-256 checksums | `aria2-next-2.7.5-checksums.sha256` |\n\nRelated report: [Motrix Next #581](https://github.com/AnInsomniacy/motrix-next/issues/581).\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnInsomniacy/aria2-next/releases/385482969/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0}}